  opens on April 19th child's play  director Lara's club burg updates this  80's horror classic for the 21st century  complete with a new take on the killer  doll Chucky this time around a young  mother played by Aubrey Plaza gifts her  son a high-tech Buddy doll without  realizing the toy isn't exactly  kid-friendly  ditching the Voodoo storyline this  remake goes full black mirror as buddy  rejects his programming and develops a  mean streak original child's play  creator Don Mancini is apparently not a  fan of this new concept but the  franchise has an aged well and an  updated reboot with plaza and red-hot  star Brian Tyree Henry could be exactly  what it needs scary stories to tell in  the dark executive producer in horror  master Guillermo del Toro selected  fellow monster lover Andre over doll as  the man to lead an adaptation of this  popular children's book series the film  combines multiple stories telling the  tale of a group of kids who must unravel  the mystery behind a wave of horrific  deaths a longtime passion project for  del Toro  even casual fans will agree he's got a  keen eye for terrifying imagery  judging from the early glimpses we've  gotten the shape of water director and /  doll have nailed the look and feel of  the books so prepare to relive your  childhood trauma  August 9th midsummer ari Astor writer  director of the insane horror film  hereditary is back in the director's  chair to terrorize us with a new  nightmare  it features Lady Macbeth's Florence Pugh  and will Poulter from Bandersnatch as a  couple who travel to a quaint Swedish  village only to be trapped in a bizarre  and dangerous competition with a pagan  cult we're giving some serious wicker  man vibes from this one and we ain't  talking about the Nick Cage not the bees  mid-summer should be another atmospheric  chiller with some good freak out moments  see it in theatres August night it  chapter 2 the second Stephen King  adaptation on our list and EMU sketti  returns to direct the sequel of 2017  it's Bill skarsgård is back as penny  wise and the adult cast is rounded out  by some heavy hitters Jessica Chastain  James McAvoy and Bill Hader who has said  scars guards penny wise is even scarier  in person it Chapter two picks up 27  years after the losers club faced off  against Pennywise the clown now they're  all grown up and ready to return home  for the final showdown it chapter 2 is  arguably the most anticipated horror  film of the year and it's in theaters  September 6  dr. sleep that's right it's Stephen King  yet again but this time we finally get a  sequel to The Shining dr. sleep stars  Ewan McGregor as a grown up Danny  Torrance who uses the shining to help  rescue other children from a cult called  the true not director Mike Flanagan has  made a name for himself on movies like  oculus Ouija origin of evil as well as  Netflix's the haunting of Hill House  series Ewan McGregor is joined by  Rebecca Ferguson and Jacob Tremblay dr.  sleep is in theaters November 8th  [Music]  [Applause]  the lighthouse it's taken a few years  but director Robert Edgar's finally  comes through with a follow-up to his  critically acclaimed 2016 horror film  The Witch Willem Dafoe and Robert  Pattinson lead this 1890s period tale  based on seafaring myths about an aging  lighthouse keeper named old shot on 35  millimeter black-and-white film stock  and using 1920s and 1940s camera  equipment both Dafoe and Pattinson have  described how excruciating and wet it  was during filming which all means that  the lighthouse could feel like a  throwback to old school horror  filmmaking it's currently set to release  sometime in 2019 little monsters Oscar  winner Lupita Nyong'o plays  schoolteacher Miss Caroline who takes  her class on a field trip to a farm  close to a military experiment while  there a zombie outbreak occurs and Miss  Caroline must save herself and her  students earlier reviews out of its  Sundance premiere praising young goes  commitment